@h1 An interactive script h1@

Author a branching game or gamebook page where character stats, a wounded-check,
and an inventory are @strong data and logic in the document strong@ — not
hand-edited for every state. This whole file builds green.

@h2 Step 1 — Character state as data h2@

A comma-free single-line record holds the scalars; a separate collection holds
the inventory, because list items can't live inside a record field (the commas
would split them).

@@@pre
#hero: { name - Vera, gold - 12, status - wounded } !!
#pack: [torch, rope, a letter you should have burned] !!
pre@@@

@h2 Step 2 — Scene vocabulary as definitions h2@

Block-form definitions with captures. Pass display text as a @strong capture strong@,
not as a body splice — a splice wraps inline content in stray paragraphs inside
your list items.

@@@pre
#scene ||title||
@h2 ::title:: h2@
scene#

#warn ||text||
@aside ⚔ ::text:: aside@
warn#

#choice ||goto, text||
@li → ::text:: (to ::goto::) li@
choice#
pre@@@

@h2 Step 3 — Scene heading and prose h2@

Splice a stat into a sentence with dotted access.

@@@pre
@scene |title The Crossroads|

@hero.name, the road forks beneath a broken signpost. You are carrying @hero.gold gold.
pre@@@

@h2 Step 4 — A conditional beat h2@

Compare a @strong string strong@ field to a literal with @code is code@.

@@@pre
(if @hero.status is wounded)
@warn |text You are wounded — the dark path may kill you.|
(end)
pre@@@

@h2 Step 5 — Choices and inventory h2@

Build the choices from the @code choice code@ definition, then iterate the pack.

@@@pre
@strong Choose: strong@
@ul
  @choice |goto village| |text Take the lit path|
  @choice |goto tower| |text Take the dark path|
ul@

@strong Pack: strong@
@ul
(each @pack as item)
@li @item li@
(end)
ul@
pre@@@

@h2 Build h2@

@@@pre
wit build scene.wit --fragment
pre@@@

@strong Result. strong@ The heading and prose splice @code Vera code@ and
@code 12 code@ into place; the wounded-check fires and prints the warning aside;
the two choices render as list items; and the pack iterates to three items — all
verified.

@h2 Pitfalls h2@

@ul
@li @strong Conditionals compare strings only. strong@ The operators are
@code is code@ and @code equals code@ (synonyms) — there is no less-than,
greater-than, @code not code@, @code and code@, @code or code@, or
@code contains code@. li@
@li @strong Model status as a string, not a number. strong@ A check for
@code low code@ compares against the literal text @code low code@; it will not
match the number @code 8 code@. Use a status string like @code wounded code@, or
an existence flag that fires when a field is present. li@
@li @strong Prose interpolation is a mirage. strong@ A capture hole written in
ordinary prose renders literally. Use dotted access
(@@@code @hero.name code@@@) in prose; a capture hole is live only inside a
definition body. li@
@li @strong Pass display text as a capture. strong@ Feeding it through a body
splice fragments it into paragraphs inside your list items — a
@@@code |text …| code@@@ capture stays clean. li@
ul@

@h2 Variations h2@

Use an existence-flag conditional; emit several scenes from a master file, as in
@a |href /docs/recipes/manuscript-chapters/| A manuscript in chapters a@; group
the choices in a wrapper definition.

@aside(class note) 💡 The shipped conditional and iteration examples are the
intended canonical grounding but currently fail to build, so treat them as
concept illustrations until repaired. Everything on this page was built from
first principles and is green. aside@

